# STATUS — cycle 5 / candidate A15 (2026-10-15)

**Mission:** boot Nuxel (Fedora 43 aarch64) on Samsung Galaxy S10+ SM-G975F
(`beyond2lte`), Exynos 9820 rev 26, bootloader G975FXXSEFUL1, TWRP 3.7.0_9-2,
ADB serial R58M75KDB2X. Earlier cycles: `STATUS.md.cycle3`,
`STATUS.md.cycle4-pre-A13`, `STATUS.md.cycle4-final`.

## Headline

**A14 is the best hardware result so far and it changes the mission completely:**
the Fedora rootfs mounted, `switch_root` started Fedora systemd 258.11 as PID 1,
and — new in A14 — **real Fedora child processes executed**: `systemd-udevd`
runs and processes kernel uevents. The A13 `pidfd_spawn`→`posix_spawn` library
repair worked; `Failed to spawn executor: Function not implemented` is gone.

Two blockers remain, both now identified with hardware evidence:

1. **The spontaneous reboot is ours.** The initramfs dead-man watchdog fires at
   its 45 s deadline and force-reboots a *healthy, running* Fedora. Measured in
   the A14 ram console: the watchdog's PID-1 probe fails with
   `sh: 1/comm: No such file or directory` at t=47.163135 s and three processes
   in this initramfs's own shell lineage (comm `init`, PIDs 3557/3558/3561) run
   the reboot notifier at t=47.171346 s, with the *normal* reboot magic `0x0` —
   no panic, no watchdog bite, HW watchdog petted throughout. Full analysis:
   `scripts/s10plus-debug-pack/captures/20261015T130509Z-A14-postfail/ANALYSIS-A14.md`.
2. **The next real blocker is cgroups, not exec.** Every systemd unit dies with
   `Failed to attach to cgroup …: No such file or directory` / `Failed at step
   CGROUP spawning …`, because no cgroup hierarchy was mounted at all
   (`cgroup2_unified=absent`). The kernel does support cgroup v2 with the
   controllers systemd needs (verified in the A15 build config:
   `CONFIG_CGROUPS=y CONFIG_MEMCG=y CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
   CONFIG_CGROUP_FREEZER=y CONFIG_CPUSETS=y`).

