## What A15 changes (BOOT partition only, initramfs only)

| Piece | Why |
|---|---|
| **dead-man watchdog removed** (`boot/initramfs/init.sh`) | it is the measured cause of the A14 reboot; a watchdog that can kill a healthy Fedora is worse than none |
| **cgroup2 mounted into the new root before `switch_root`** | fixes `Failed at step CGROUP` for every systemd unit (A14 measurement) |
| **first light re-done** (`tools/s10plus/nuxel-fb-phone.c`) | logs every fb geometry field to kmsg; paints *every* buffer of the 1440x6080 virtual framebuffer; unmistakable bright frame (colour bars + big NUXEL wordmark + white-outlined penguin on deep blue, no full-white AMOLED frame); 12-frame spinning penguin; prints `NUXEL_FB_ANIM_DONE` so the init logs `FIRSTLIGHT_ANIMATION_DONE` |
| kernel source/defconfig/DTB/header | **unchanged** from A12 → the only kernel difference is the embedded initramfs |

## Build-environment defect found and fixed (cycle 5)

The container's kernel trees `/b/src` and `/b/src2` are **silently truncated
extractions** — `scripts/Kbuild.include` was 0 bytes, which is exactly why any
`make … defconfig` failed with `make: *** empty variable name. Stop.`
(`build := -f $(srctree)/scripts/Makefile.build obj` lives in that file, so
`$(build)` expanded to nothing and kbuild ran `make =scripts/basic`). The A15
kernel was therefore built from a **fresh extraction of `/b/kernel.tar.gz`**
(69,687 files) with verified non-empty critical files.

Also: `tools/kernel-relax-werror.sh` deletes `-Werror` tokens, leaving dangling
backslash continuations in the top-level Makefile, and a naive
`-Werror`→`-Wno-error` rewrite yields `-Wno-error-implicit-function-declaration`,
which GCC 15 rejects as an **unknown option (a hard error)**. A15 uses a
structure-preserving rewrite (`.scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/relax-werror.sh`).

