## Standing risks
* No real stock BOOT backup (`backups/s10plus/boot-original.img` is a `DUMMY`).
  RECOVERY is untouched and backed up; every write is BOOT-only; USERDATA has
  never been written (A13/A14 write *into* the mounted Fedora rootfs, never to
  the raw image).
* `reboot -f` is the escalation path if a test hangs; the operator's
  POWER+VOLUMEDOWN combo and TWRP remain available.
